* Parents: 4200215e7 (lift) + 93c808f7e (b1-seal local tip, carrying the span through PR #173). 32 files conflicted (~80 hunks; the span's S2b/S3b browser ward work met lift's per-face custody), resolved by hunk; 5 carriers normalized twice to canonical.
* THE COLLISION AND ITS COMPOSITION (worth the controller's read): lift rested the persona root in the face's own tree (`face-root/<G>`, ward acts via `faceWardRows`); span's S2b rests it under a per-face WARD keyed by handle (`ward/h<N>/slots|persona-root`, roster `persona-root-roster` = index + public key under the place tree). Merged: the ward holds the root (lift's own carrier named that move as owed); `face-root/<G>` retires and every door refuses it `ward-needs-fresh-unlock`; the roster rests under the place tree (lift's HANDLE_ROW no longer lists it; its codec is span's); lift's one-root-per-face holds at the mint and slot (`refuseOtherHandle`, h0 only); every other D row stays per face, and span's new `vessel-face-tag/<G>` joins the face rows (FACE_ROWS). A founding's tag secret mints before the group names the tree, so `browserVesselFaceTagDoor(idb, ward, rowFace)` seals it under the unnamed founder face (cured rest-before-reload's `no-custody-slot` boot red). Ward APIs take span's signatures (handleIndex + WardRoute); lift callers pass 0 (the worn face's handle). The vessel host asks ward routes through the ceremony with `wardAskWords(act, kind)`; the ceremony paints those words; a fleet join carries `ward: { route: askWardOf(conn) }`; span's `wardAsk` hello flag and page ward form dropped (lift's ceremony stands).
* OWED (named in seat-harness residuals + browser-vessel-lift slice 3): re-key the browser ward and roster by PersonaGroup (they still name the face `h0`); lift's face-absent/no-tree checks at the root mint went with the root's move (no face gate on the ward mint now).
* Tests trued to the composition (span tests bind the face's tree before tag rows; lift tests read the root under the ward; ward-root r4/r4b pre-stand the founder face so the ward bind/retype path stays exercised); fleet-join's five-bind test takes a 90 s timeout (it timed out at 30 s once under the full package run, 11/11 alone).
